<title>BELGIUM: Council agrees common position on public markets.</title>
<headline>Council agrees common position on public markets.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Internal Market Council struck a common position on Tuesday on a proposal to adapt the EU's public procurement directives to take account of the Government Procurement Agreement operated within the World Trade Organisation.</p>
<p>The proposal concerned the directives on the so-called &quot;excluded sectors&quot; of water, energy, transport and telecommunications.</p>
<p>The modifications were made to ensure that third country suppliers do not enjoy better access to contracts than Community suppliers and to introduce more flexibility into the technical dialogue between suppliers and procurement entities.</p>
</text>
